Disable data reporting at compile time -- COMMON half (LW-M1-02).

Split out of upstream's patches/disable-data-reporting-at-compile-time.patch,
which is a straddler: it mixes toolkit/python hunks that are built on every
target with browser/-only hunks. This file holds the target-independent hunks;
patches/disable-data-reporting-desktop.patch holds the browser/ hunks and the
hunks whose context only exists in the desktop Firefox version. common + desktop
together are byte-for-byte upstream's current patch.

LISTED IN desktop.txt, NOT common.txt, SINCE THE FIREFOX 157 DESKTOP MERGE.
Desktop builds firefox-157.0; Android builds firefox-153.0esr (version.android)
and its patched tree is held byte-identical to the pre-merge one. So Android
does not apply this file: it applies the pre-merge common half verbatim,
patches/android/disable-data-reporting-common-esr.patch, followed by
patches/android/disable-data-reporting-android.patch (also pre-merge bytes),
both in assets/patches/android.txt. Re-merge this file into common.txt (and drop
the -esr copy) when Android moves to an ESR >= 157.

What is here:
  python/mach/mach/telemetry.py                    mach telemetry, target-independent
  toolkit/components/telemetry/core/Telemetry.cpp  TelemetryImpl never records
  toolkit/library/rust/gkrust-features.mozbuild    glean_disable_upload for official builds
  toolkit/components/telemetry/core/Stopwatch.cpp,
  toolkit/components/telemetry/core/TelemetryUserInteraction.{cpp,h}
                                                   upstream fb4c7a32: with telemetry off,
                                                   UserInteraction.* calls stop logging
                                                   "cannot be recorded" errors. This
                                                   replaces the old tabbrowser.js hunk
                                                   (dropped upstream in a1bd18fa).

What is NOT here any more, and why (both became version-specific at 157):
  python/sites/mach.txt     pins the glean-sdk version (68.0.1 on 157, 67.3.2 on
                            153esr) -> the 157 hunk is in the desktop half; the
                            153esr hunk is in disable-data-reporting-common-esr.
  glean disable hunks       157: upstream patches third_party/rust/glean-core
                            (lib.rs, core/mod.rs) -> desktop half; the matching
                            .cargo-checksum.json hashes rewritten by
                            scripts/librewolf-patches.py are the 157 hashes and do
                            NOT match the 153esr files.
                            153esr: toolkit/components/glean/src/init/mod.rs
                            (use_core_mps / enable_internal_pings false), kept in
                            disable-data-reporting-common-esr; on 157 that code
                            became a builder and the hunk rejects.

WHERE THE ANDROID OFF SWITCH LIVES -- READ THIS BEFORE ASSUMING THIS PATCH IS
ENOUGH ON ANDROID.

The compile-time data-reporting switch is *not* in this patch. It is
MOZ_DATA_REPORTING, computed at toolkit/moz.configure:3493-3507 as

    telemetry or healthreport or crashreporter or normandy

from four per-project inputs. The front end supplies two of them, and each front
end supplies its own:

  browser/moz.configure:6,10       MOZ_SERVICES_HEALTHREPORT True, MOZ_NORMANDY True
                                   -> flipped to False by the DESKTOP half.
  mobile/android/moz.configure:131 MOZ_NORMANDY False               (already off)
  mobile/android/moz.configure:132 MOZ_SERVICES_HEALTHREPORT True   (still ON)

So on Android the common half alone (today: its 153esr copy,
patches/android/disable-data-reporting-common-esr.patch) leaves
MOZ_SERVICES_HEALTHREPORT defined and MOZ_DATA_REPORTING with it. That is
closed by

    patches/android/disable-data-reporting-android.patch   (assets/patches/android.txt)

which must be applied alongside the common half for every Android build. Do not try to
close it from the mozconfig: assets/mozconfig.android's
`mk_add_options MOZ_SERVICES_HEALTHREPORT=0` is make-level only
(python/mozbuild/mozbuild/mozconfig.py routes mk_add_options into make_extra and
never into configure's environment), and an `export` would make configure die on
the implied/explicit conflict with mobile/android/moz.configure:132.

